{"sections":[],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/eventmacros\/event(name:consent:version:)"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@attached"},{"kind":"text","text":"(extension, conformances: "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Event","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Event","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Events5EventP"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Encodable","preciseIdentifier":"s:SE"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Decodable","preciseIdentifier":"s:Se"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"__DiscoverableEvent"},{"kind":"text","text":", names: named(name), named(consentCategory), named(schemaVersion), named(schema), named(constraintViolation), named(CodingKeys), named(encode(to:)), named(init(from:)), named(decodeValue), named(decodeIfPresentValue), named(requireCodable), named(codableRequirements)) "},{"kind":"attribute","text":"@attached"},{"kind":"text","text":"(peer) "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"macro"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Event"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"name"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"kind":"text","text":"? = nil, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"consent"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/ConsentCategory","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"ConsentCategory","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Events15ConsentCategoryV"},{"kind":"text","text":"? = nil, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"version"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"},{"kind":"text","text":" = 1)"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"parameters","parameters":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The name destinations record the event under, a string literal; the type’s name when"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":". No other event in the program may share it, whatever its version."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"name"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The purpose the event is collected for; ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/ConsentCategory\/analytics","type":"reference"},{"text":" when ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"consent"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The schema version, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Event.schemaVersion"},{"type":"text","text":": a positive integer literal, raised for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each breaking change; 1 by default."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"version"}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"overview","level":2},{"type":"codeListing","code":["import EventMacros","","@Event(name: \"signed_up\", consent: .functional, version: 2)","struct SignedUp {","    var plan: String","    var seats: Int?","    var email: Sensitive<String>","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The macro adds a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nonisolated"},{"type":"text","text":" extension, so the conformance works off the main actor, where"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the tracker encodes events, even when the struct is marked "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@MainActor"},{"type":"text","text":"; such a struct’s stored"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"properties must then be "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sendable"},{"type":"text","text":". The extension holds:"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"static var name"},{"text":": ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"name"},{"text":" when it is given; otherwise the type’s name,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"String(describing: Self.self)"},{"text":", the value of ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Event"},{"text":"’s default.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"static var consentCategory"},{"type":"text","text":", when "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"consent"},{"type":"text","text":" is given; otherwise "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/ConsentCategory\/analytics","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"static var schemaVersion","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", when ","type":"text"},{"code":"version","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is given; otherwise 1, ","type":"text"},{"code":"Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"’s default.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"static var schema"},{"type":"text","text":": an "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/EventSchema","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" with the event’s name, version and each stored"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"property’s name, type as written, optionality, whether it has a default value and validation"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"keywords (its "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Refined","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" type’s rule’s, then those "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/EventMacros\/documentation\/EventMacros\/Constrained(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" declares), in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"declaration order. A property of a raw-value enum gets its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/EventSchema\/Enumeration","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", the cases’ raw values. The macro lists them when the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"enum is declared inside the struct, and reads them from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"allCases"},{"type":"text","text":" for one declared elsewhere"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"or with a case under "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"#if"},{"type":"text","text":". An enum declared elsewhere needs "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CaseIterable"},{"type":"text","text":" for a tracking"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"plan to check its values; without it, and for a typealias of an enum, the plan accepts any"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"value."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"constraintViolation()"},{"type":"text","text":", when a property declares constraints with "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/EventMacros\/documentation\/EventMacros\/Constrained(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":": the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"first property, in declaration order, whose value breaks one, which a tracker rejects."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"CodingKeys","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"encode(to:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"init(from:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and the private functions it reads some types"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"through, which write a keyed container of the stored"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"properties, each under its name, and read each back by its name, as a hand-written"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"conformance would. A store writes the container as a CBOR map. An optional property’s "},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is left out, and an optional property missing from the map reads as "},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"; one with a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"default value reads as that value, so its "},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is written. A "},{"code":"Date","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" property, optional or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not, and each date in a "},{"code":"[Date]","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"code":"[Date?]","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" property, is written as the seconds since 2001"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it stores, so it reads back exactly. A "},{"code":"Date","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" inside a "},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" type of your own takes the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"CBOR package’s own form, seconds since 1970, and reads back to within a rounding of a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"microsecond’s scale. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Sensitive"},{"type":"text","text":" property goes through its own conformance, so only a store writes its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"value."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Beside the struct the macro adds a private record, which the compiler places in the binary so","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/DiscoveredEvent\/all","isActive":true},{"text":" lists the event at run time, and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SegmentStore()"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DatabaseStore(database:)"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrackingPlan()"},{"text":" take it without a list. The record holds the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"struct as an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"__DiscoverableEvent"},{"text":", an underscored protocol the macro conforms it to and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"discovery reads, which the event’s code doesn’t use. A generic struct, or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one nested in a generic type’s declaration, gets no record, as a record holds one concrete","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"type: it isn’t discovered, and the macro adds a note saying to list it. So does one in an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"extension that names the type’s generic arguments (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"extension Box<Int>"},{"text":") or has a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"where"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"clause. A struct declared in a plain extension of a generic type doesn’t compile (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"static stored properties not supported in generic types"},{"text":"), as the extension doesn’t say the type is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"generic; declare it outside the generic type.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Beside the record the macro adds a function whose symbol is named for the event’s name,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$linkerset_kind_65766E74_key_"},{"type":"text","text":" and the name, its ASCII letters and digits as they are and every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"other byte as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_"},{"type":"text","text":" and two hex digits. Two events of one name in one linked image, whatever their"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"versions, define that symbol twice and fail to build: in one module the compiler refuses the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"second, and across the modules of one executable or library the linker does, naming the symbol."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The check doesn’t reach across images: a dynamic library, a library opened with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dlopen"},{"type":"text","text":", or a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"module linked into two images is caught only when a store or tracking plan reads"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/DiscoveredEvent\/all"},{"type":"text","text":" and throws for the duplicate name. A struct inside a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"private"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"fileprivate"},{"type":"text","text":" type or extension gets no such function, as its symbol would be local to the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"file, so only those run-time errors check its name. The name is the one "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"name"},{"type":"text","text":" gives, or the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"type’s, and the extension always declares it as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"name"},{"type":"text","text":", so the name can’t differ from the one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"checked: a struct that declares a static "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"name"},{"type":"text","text":" itself is a compile error, with a Fix-It that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"moves a string literal into "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"name"},{"type":"text","text":", and one declared in an extension or under "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"#if"},{"type":"text","text":" is a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"redeclaration."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Every stored instance property is encoded, and needs a type annotation. Static and computed","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"properties are left out, and so is a ","type":"text"},{"code":"let","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with an initial value, which every value shares.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The struct keeps its memberwise initializer.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A stored property whose type isn’t "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Codable"},{"type":"text","text":" is a compile error naming it:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"static method 'requireCodable(bad:)' requires that 'Foo' conform to 'Decodable'"},{"type":"text","text":" for a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"property "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"bad"},{"type":"text","text":" of type "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Foo"},{"type":"text","text":". A raw-value enum is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Codable"},{"type":"text","text":", written as its raw value, once it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"declares the conformance ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"enum Reason: String, Codable"},{"type":"text","text":"). One declared inside the struct must"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"list it in its inheritance clause, even when an extension adds it, since the macro sees only"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the struct; without it, the error is the macro’s own, at that clause. Applying the macro to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"anything but a struct, a property with no type annotation, a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lazy"},{"type":"text","text":" property, a destructuring"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"pattern, a name that isn’t a non-empty string literal, a static "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"name"},{"type":"text","text":" declared in the struct"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and a version that isn’t a positive integer literal are compile errors too."}]},{"text":"Changing an event","type":"heading","anchor":"Changing-an-event","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A store may still hold records written before an event’s stored properties changed: an app","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"updates with records on disk it hasn’t delivered. ","type":"text"},{"code":"version","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" counts the changes those records","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"can’t be read through, and only those. Each record carries the version it was stored at, and a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"store drops one stored at another version than the type’s now without reading it, reporting the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"event and both versions (","type":"text"},{"code":"DropReport.versionMismatch","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"). A tracking plan’s check","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(module ","type":"text"},{"code":"TrackingPlans","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") fails on a change that needs a new version while the version stayed","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the same, naming the event, the property and the change.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"These changes are compatible. Keep the version, and the records stored before the change are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"read by each property’s name, in any order:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["\/\/ Version 1, as released.","@Event(name: \"checkout_started\")","struct CheckoutStarted {","    var cartSize: Int","    var screen: String","}","","\/\/ Still version 1: a record stored above reads with coupon nil, currency \"USD\" and screen","\/\/ skipped.","@Event(name: \"checkout_started\")","struct CheckoutStarted {","    var cartSize: Int","    var coupon: String?          \/\/ an optional property added: nil","    var currency: String = \"USD\" \/\/ a property with a default value added: the default","                                 \/\/ screen removed: its stored value is skipped","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"These changes are breaking. Raise the version with each, and the records stored at the earlier","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one are dropped and reported:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["@Event(name: \"checkout_started\", version: 2)","struct CheckoutStarted {","    var cartSize: Double  \/\/ a property's type changed (it was Int)","    var coupon: String    \/\/ an optional property made required (it was String?)","    var paymentMethod: String \/\/ a required property added, with no default value","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A version raised for a change whose bytes would still read, such as a property that keeps its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"type but changes its meaning, drops the earlier records all the same, so they are never read","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"as the new shape. Records are never migrated from one version to another.","type":"text"}]}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/EventMacros\/documentation\/EventMacros\/Event(name:consent:version:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"abstract":[{"text":"Makes a struct an event: derives its ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Event"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Codable"},{"text":" conformances, its name and its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/EventSchema"},{"text":" from its declaration.","type":"text"}],"metadata":{"externalID":"s:11EventMacros0A04name7consent7versionySSSg_6Events15ConsentCategoryVSgSitcfm","roleHeading":"Macro","fragments":[{"text":"macro","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Event","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"name","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"text":"?, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"consent","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ConsentCategory","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Events15ConsentCategoryV"},{"text":"?, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"version","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"Event.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/EventMacros\/Event.swift#L157"},"title":"Event(name:consent:version:)","role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"EventMacros"}],"symbolKind":"macro"},"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/EventMacros\/documentation\/EventMacros"]]},"references":{"doc://EventMacros/documentation/EventMacros":{"url":"\/documentation\/eventmacros","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/EventMacros\/documentation\/EventMacros","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"EventMacros","abstract":[{"text":"Derive an event’s conformances, name and schema from its struct declaration, and declare the constraints its properties satisfy.","type":"text"}]},"doc://Events/documentation/Events/EventSchema/Enumeration":{"url":"\/documentation\/events\/eventschema\/enumeration","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/EventSchema\/Enumeration","abstract":[{"text":"The raw values a property of a raw-value enum is written as: the enum’s name, its raw value’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"type and, where they are known, every case’s raw value.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Enumeration"}],"title":"EventSchema.Enumeration","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Enumeration"}]},"doc://Events/documentation/Events/Refined":{"url":"\/documentation\/events\/refined","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Refined"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Refined"}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Refined","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A value that satisfies every constraint of ","type":"text"},{"code":"Rule","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", checked once as it is made, so a property of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"this type can’t hold one that doesn’t.","type":"text"}],"title":"Refined"},"doc://Events/documentation/Events/ConsentCategory/analytics":{"url":"\/documentation\/events\/consentcategory\/analytics","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/ConsentCategory\/analytics","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Measuring how the product is used: the category of every event that names no other."}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"analytics","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ConsentCategory","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Events15ConsentCategoryV"}],"title":"analytics"},"doc://EventMacros/documentation/EventMacros/Constrained(_:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/eventmacros\/constrained(_:)","fragments":[{"text":"macro","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Constrained","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:6Events17ValidationKeywordO","text":"ValidationKeyword","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"...)","kind":"text"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/EventMacros\/documentation\/EventMacros\/Constrained(_:)","title":"Constrained(_:)","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Declares the constraints a stored property of an ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" struct satisfies, which ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"checks and lists in the event’s schema.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://Events/documentation/Events/DiscoveredEvent/all":{"url":"\/documentation\/events\/discoveredevent\/all","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/DiscoveredEvent\/all","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Every event type the program links, ordered by the UTF-8 bytes of their names, then by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"version, then by the types’ fully qualified names."}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"all"},{"kind":"text","text":": ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Events15DiscoveredEventV","text":"DiscoveredEvent"},{"kind":"text","text":"]"}],"title":"all"},"doc://Events/documentation/Events/Sensitive":{"url":"\/documentation\/events\/sensitive","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Sensitive","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Sensitive","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","title":"Sensitive","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A property value that a destination reads only through the record it arrived in, and not at all","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"once the record is redacted.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Sensitive"},"doc://EventMacros/documentation/EventMacros/Event(name:consent:version:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/eventmacros\/event(name:consent:version:)","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/EventMacros\/documentation\/EventMacros\/Event(name:consent:version:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Makes a struct an event: derives its "},{"code":"Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" conformances, its name and its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/EventSchema"},{"type":"text","text":" from its declaration."}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"macro","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Event","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"name","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"text":"?, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"consent","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ConsentCategory","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Events15ConsentCategoryV"},{"text":"?, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"version","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"title":"Event(name:consent:version:)"},"doc://Events/documentation/Events/Event":{"url":"\/documentation\/events\/event","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Event","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Event","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Event","title":"Event","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Something that happened, recorded as a typed value."}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://Events/documentation/Events/ConsentCategory":{"url":"\/documentation\/events\/consentcategory","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/ConsentCategory","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The purpose an event is collected for, which the user consents to or refuses: analytics,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"advertising and the like."}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ConsentCategory","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"ConsentCategory","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ConsentCategory","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Events/documentation/Events/EventSchema":{"url":"\/documentation\/events\/eventschema","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"EventSchema","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EventSchema","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/EventSchema","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The shape of an event type: its name, its schema version, its consent category and its stored"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"properties in declaration order, as a value tooling reads."}],"kind":"symbol","title":"EventSchema"}}}